// The landing page of the documentation. Each topic is defined by the header that declares it.
// This file contains prose only. Nothing here is compiled, and the headers do not repeat it.

/// \mainpage STDCORELIB
///
/// A C++17 support library for functionality that the standard library leaves to the platform.
///
/// Most components exist because their implementation differs between Windows and other
/// platforms: console color, UTF-8 output on a Windows console, starting a child process, and
/// loading a shared object. The remaining components are containers and utilities that projects
/// otherwise reimplement repeatedly.
///
/// \section main_conventions Conventions
///
/// \li <b>Every \c std::string is UTF-8.</b> This applies to arguments, environment variables, log
///     messages and the output of a child process. On Windows, strings are converted at the system
///     call rather than through the system code page. Text in any script therefore survives the
///     round trip. A \c std::filesystem::path is the exception, because it uses the native
///     encoding of its platform.
/// \li <b>A failure is reported through the return value.</b> A function returns \c std::optional
///     if a failure has no further description, and \c std::error_code if it has one. A function
///     that throws documents the exception.
/// \li <b>RTTI is not required.</b> stdc::type_id and stdc::any identify a type without \c typeid,
///     and the library is built with \c -fno-rtti to verify this property.
/// \li Components are header-only if possible and compiled otherwise. The library depends only on
///     the standard library.
///
/// \section main_organization Organization
///
/// The Components page lists every part of the library, each with a description and an example
/// and each defined by the header that declares it. The README describes building the library
/// and linking against it.
